text='''# W05 postseal source corrections

This report-only successor preserves source head `43f7cf6e8681fa617b5d6d3529d94d537ca01f0d` and sealed correction head `5156d92bec6bd885ca8bae3c5e18bfdce0069176`. The exact new published head is recorded after ordinary push in the single private `.temp/w05-postseal-source-corrections-v1/HANDOFF.json`. Coordinator integration and final acceptance remain separate.

The selected ledger is `core/decisions.json`, `core/proposals.json`, `core/evidence.json` and `core/proposal-lineage.json`. It accounts for CASES frozen W05 cases, OCCURRENCES occurrence memberships, PROPOSALS current proposals and ORIGINAL authentic original proposal lineages. CHANGED_D decision records and CHANGED_P full payloads have new reviewed bytes; the remaining UNCHANGED_D decision objects and UNCHANGED_P proposal objects retain their exact predecessor content. All OLD_E original evidence objects remain, with TOTAL_E current entries. Counts measure accounting, not identity resolution or release approval.

The bounded source changes are:

- BSA source case70 (zero-based), `CM_NAME:8ba1df295abb60b7fb8cd7e12f80b861e3d2e7634dd64e3bfb7e88df0db0fd08`, is BSK JCM201/TOGOM194. Its literal 50 g Fraction V input has unknown final volume. The proposal does not infer 50 g/L, ADC/OADC context, catalogue identity or release of the separate #1222 quantity hold or inherited A7030 limitations. Four other linked BSA decisions receive current review metadata without expanded scientific scope.
- Marine Broth 2216 retains COMPLETE coverage of all 16 nominal printed dry-product inputs and their quantities. The manufacturer qualifies the printed formula as approximate and adjustable to meet performance criteria. Water remains outside the dry product; unknown salt forms and lot composition are not guessed. The prior agar-only inference was already withdrawn at the predecessor; its historical record is preserved.
- Three dependent MicrobeDecoder preparation proposals now retain literal `rumen fluid` with UNMAPPED component reference scope and no component identifier. Their raw primary database rows do not establish the clarified-fluid bridge. This correction does not infer untreated fluid. The separate JCM1423/1424 to JCM266 clarification observations and their distinct owner proposal remain intact. Full-text access failures and exact available observations are recorded.

The Tris salt already has NARROW_MATCH to CHEBI:9754 with exact CAS1185-53-1 in the predecessor. No additional Tris edit or history event is made. Both historical two-row and current three-row native projections are retained; the latter includes the local registry identity. Seven weighed salt contexts are not generalized to all 16 case occurrences.

The complete #1237 applicability ledger covers 26 frozen rows and 28 finding IDs, six captured comment extensions and the additional body groups. `chemical-ledger-remediation-v1/family-applicability-audit-v2.json` is the selected ledger. The initial ledger remains immutable; four other-origin explanatory captions were corrected after independent findings, with every source disposition, ID and scientific payload unchanged. HEPES, Wolfe and 95% ethanol remain conditional: omitted form, carrier, pH or concentration basis proves neither difference nor equality. Root retains DAIGO, phosphate, Hutner, Columbia, ten-vitamin and other whole-union reconciliation ownership. No arbitrary owner or tombstone is selected.

Actual primary authors were `/root/materials_research` (five BSA cases, one payload), `/root/media_research` (two Marine Broth cases, one payload), and `/root/chemicals_research` (one linked clarified-rumen decision, three dependent parent payloads, and current family applicability). `/root/final_skeptical` independently reviewed all eight changed decisions and all five complete changed payloads with their primary sources. Its separately attributed child `/root/final_skeptical/preservation_audit` reviewed the complete tracker and unchanged chemical/Tris scope; its precise entry and case bindings are published. The root compiled envelopes and checks and is not represented as an independent scientific reviewer.

The native outcome auditor, guarded writer, closed-schema checks and full substituted owner/component corpus checks validate these exact selected bytes. All 142 full payloads pass strict validation; the isolated corpus contains 3,029 records. Full native row comparisons show four provenance-only curator-token changes (BSA and the three rumen parent rows), as required by authentic appended history. All other cells and row identities remain unchanged; the Marine row is entirely unchanged. The first overstrict local comparison wrapper failure and corrected diagnostic are preserved. No producer or gate was changed, and no downstream export was rebuilt.

`finding-register.json` retains all original 18 findings and authentic prior dispositions, deduplicates the new source corrections against filed issues, and records the report-only ledger finding and rereview. No new MappingEvidence entries or bulk evidence-type replacement are introduced. Original human evidence and ComponentEvidence enum differences remain. Exact unchanged prior source reviews retain their original attribution and limitations; they are not reauthored or promoted to whole-owner approval.

All primary captures retain their exact bytes and original acquisition timestamps. Public copies of the private packets preserve their recorded path/hash identities; `source-ledger.json` maps the selected public evidence and actual scopes. Every prior review, capture, manifest and the sealed 22-family comparison remains preserved. Source-specific, owner, role and export holds remain effective. No maintained data, schema, workflow, pin, gate, merge, GitHub write, paid provider or new external session is part of this successor.
'''
